      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $U∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(U\\ge 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "An exponential random variable $U$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nU∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(U\\ge 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U\\ge 3) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-2u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2u}{|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-6} \\\\  & ≈0.0025\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
